00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.980
Coding agents just saved a production library release by catching five release blocking bugs

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.180
that the author missed at an estimated $149 cost.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:34.800
Simon Willison ran Clawed Fable through a final pre-release review of SQLite-utils 4.0 RC1.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.320
The agent produced a report that flagged five release blockers.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:45.960
One example was a deleteware method that never committed and left the connection in an open transaction state.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:54.460
Over 37 prompts and 34 commits, the agent rewrote transaction handling so every right method now commits automatically

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:58.400
unless an explicit atomic or begin context is active.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:08.380
It also added DB begin, commit, and rollback helpers plus updated documentation for Python 3.12 auto commit connections.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:16.700
Two further edge cases in DB query surfaced during a follow-up GPT 5.5 review and were fixed.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:23.640
The full effort cost an estimated $149.25 on the Clawed Max Plan.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:33.000
This week's model updates start with a new adapter for the Quinn family, a 10 megabyte Laura on Quinn 3.5 to 4B.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:40.260
Reads internal activations to decide whether to answer directly, call web search or retrieve from local documents.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:47.820
It refuses to fabricate when verification fails and improved error detection by deprime 0.46.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.500
Private queries sent to public search dropped from 22% to 10%.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:02:07.320
The adapter runs locally via MLX on Apple Silicon or GGUF in llama.cpp or O llama and ships under Apache 2.0 with full weights and training code.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:14.440
Next, Jun Yang Lin, the former technical lead on Quinn, published an essay on hybrid thinking limits.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:20.240
He described where Quinn 3 hybrid thinking modes and dynamic budgets fell short in practice.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:26.940
Lin now favors agentic reinforcement learning infrastructure over further reasoning mode tuning.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:38.220
The piece highlights reward hacking risks that appear once agent trajectories lengthen and the added difficulty of building stable agent training loops versus single turn reasoning.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:49.720
A separate guide on mark tech posts surveys open source models that convert enterprise PDFs, scans and slide decks into schema driven JSON on local hardware.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:55.700
